  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "The current best (config_003: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat; acc 0.619) uses PCA—a linear, untrained dimensionality reduction—as the RNA encoder. The only other dimension we've tested is aggregation (avgpool > transformer), while the RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy remain unexplored. Config_011 changes exactly one variable (RNA encoder: pca_n2000 → scvi_n200) while holding everything else fixed (multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat), giving a clean single-factor comparison. This tests whether a nonlinear, learned RNA representation (scVI) captures structure that PCA misses, which is a fundamental design decision for cellular profiling. If scvi_n200 significantly outperforms PCA, it signals that representation quality on the RNA side is a major lever and justifies further exploration (e.g., scgpt). If it does not, PCA is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward image-encoder or fusion questions. Under a limited budget, isolating the RNA-encoder effect is the highest-information next step because it addresses the most basic representational assumption in the current best model."
}

